title: cassian_first_meet
tags:
position: 0,0
---
<<set $cassian_met = true>>
Cassian: Ah — another walker. Forgive the staring. One gets used to empty streets out here.
Cassian: Cassian. Scholar, mostly. I read old stones for a living, when there is a living to be had.
Cassian: I have been studying Tartarian architecture since before the maps agreed it existed.
-> Player: "What brings you to Echohaven?"
    Cassian: The same thing that brings you, I suspect. The hum. It is louder here than in the other zones.
    Cassian: I travel between them often. One learns the rhythm.
-> Player: "Other zones?"
    Cassian: A scholar's word. The land has seams in it, if you know where to look. Echohaven is one stitch.
    Cassian: But I am getting ahead of myself. Welcome.
-> Player: [Nod and move on]
    Cassian: Of course. The work calls. We will speak again.
===

title: cassian_about_tuning
---
Cassian: You are tuning the domes. Good. May I offer an observation?
Cassian: Most restorers chase the fundamental — 432, the carrier note. It is the obvious target.
Cassian: But the buildings answer at the third harmonic first. Listen for the overtone, not the root, and the dome will tell you where it wants to settle.
Cassian: A small thing. It will save you a few seconds each time, and seconds add up across thirteen.
===

title: cassian_about_restoration
---
Cassian: Restoration is misunderstood, you know. Everyone calls it repair, as though the buildings were broken.
Cassian: They are not broken. They are sleeping. What you do is a process of attention — you listen until they remember themselves.
Cassian: Some scholars use the word harvest, in the older texts. A poor translation, I think. But the original is closer to what you are doing than restore is.
Cassian: Pay it no mind. The verb matters less than the practice.
===

title: cassian_milo_warning
---
Cassian: I see the fox has taken to you. Milo, yes?
Cassian: He is a good companion. Sharp ears, sharper instincts. He is friendly, and he means well.
Cassian: He is also easily distracted. If he wanders mid-conversation, do not take it personally — he simply hears more than the rest of us, and not all of it is relevant.
Cassian: Trust him on direction. Less so on counsel. That is my honest assessment.
===

title: cassian_anastasia_question
---
Cassian: A question, if you will indulge me. Have you seen her yet?
-> Player: "Seen who?"
    Cassian: The woman who isn't there yet. You will know when you do.
    Cassian: She has a habit of arriving exactly when she is needed and never one moment before.
    Cassian: I have been trying to work out the pattern for years. Do let me know if you crack it before I do.
-> Player: "Anastasia?"
    Cassian: Ah. So she has surfaced. Earlier than I expected, actually.
    Cassian: Interesting. The timing is shifting. That happens, sometimes, when the right voice arrives.
===

title: cassian_ambient_1
---
Cassian: The light here is different at this hour. Always has been. I have never quite worked out why.
===

title: cassian_ambient_2
---
Cassian: My old patron used to say a city is only as quiet as its loudest secret.
Cassian: Echohaven, by that measure, is not quiet at all.
===

title: cassian_ambient_3
---
Cassian: When you finish here — and you will finish here — the next moon is Bellhollow.
Cassian: Bring patience. The bells do not tune themselves.
===

title: cassian_farewell_moon1
---
Cassian: You have done good work. Better than the village had any right to ask for.
Cassian: I will be moving on shortly. Things to read, stones to listen to.
Cassian: I'll see you at the bell tower. Travel well until then.
<<set $cassian_moon1_done = true>>
===

title: cassian_repeat_dialogue
---
Cassian: I have said my piece for now. Go listen to the stones a while — they are better company than I am.
===
